Hash Tables cannot read through Data in an ordered sequence
Hash Table also require an excessive amount of Empty Space

Binary Search Trees- Data Structure utilizing a Binary Search to find
and print an ordered sequence of data

Binary Search Trees allow for data to maintain it's order.

Binary Search Trees are a combination of a Binary Search and a Linked List

The first Node of a Binary Tree is referred to as a Root Node
The Root will always have two Leaf Nodes that act as references
The structure is Hierarchical rather than linear, so Recursion is essential for
traversal. 

A Complete Binary Tree: Every Node either has 0 or 2 Sub Nodes


Depth-First searches: A means of Traversal of Trees, where you reach the bottom nodes
then backtrack to the Root

Trees are Organized into Roots, Leafs, and Sub-Trees

The Height and Depth of Trees: How many levels of Nodes (Depth) or
the Number of Edges = # of Nodes - 1 (Depth)

A Binary Search Tree only traverses from Right to Left, Descending from
a Root

